      {
        "h": "The make-up behind Hammer's monsters",
        "p": "The National Science and Media Museum in Bradford holds the Ashton &amp; Leakey Collection: sketches, prosthetics, glass eyes and fangs from Hammer make-up artists Roy Ashton and Phil Leakey, covering <em>The Curse of Frankenstein</em> (1957), <em>Dracula</em> (1958), <em>The Mummy</em> (1959) and <em>The Gorgon</em> (1964). Great British Life reports the museum is opening the collection up.",
        "src": "Science Museum Group",
